DESCRIPTION >
    Immutable incoming Jitsu delivery observations. Occurrence key is tenant_id, envelope_hash, event_index.
    Queue retries share an occurrence key. Repeated upstream deliveries can have different occurrence keys.
    Readers must deduplicate occurrences and choose source heads by event kind, message ID and source version.
    Reject conflicting hashes. delivery_event_id also identifies retries of the same upstream batch.

SCHEMA >
    `tenant_id` String `json:$.tenant_id`,
    `envelope_hash` String `json:$.envelope_hash`,
    `event_index` UInt32 `json:$.event_index`,
    `delivery_event_id` String `json:$.delivery_event_id`,
    `message_id` String `json:$.message_id`,
    `event_kind` String `json:$.event_kind`,
    `received_at` DateTime64(3) `json:$.received_at`,
    `observation_json` String `json:$.observation_json`,
    `observation_hash` String `json:$.observation_hash`

ENGINE MergeTree
ENGINE_SORTING_KEY tenant_id, envelope_hash, event_index

TOKEN v1_facts_runtime READ
TOKEN v1_facts_runtime APPEND
